infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Cost profile: middleware vs DI
  desc Middleware cost recurs on every request; DI cost is paid once at startup
  compares
    - label Middleware - paid per request, forever
      children
        - label p50 +0.3-0.5ms on a 12-15 layer chain
          desc auth, logging, body parse, compression, CORS, helmet, rate limit - each layer adds single-digit microseconds
        - label p99 +1-3ms
          desc once GC and a slow async layer like an audit log are in play
        - label Multiplied by every request
          desc a middleware mistake taxes throughput on each of millions of requests
    - label DI wiring - paid once at startup
      children
        - label Boot tens to low-hundreds of ms
          desc a NestJS app with a few hundred providers builds its whole object graph at boot
        - label Near-zero per-request wiring
          desc requests are served by singletons already constructed - almost no ongoing cost
        - label Paid once at boot
          desc a DI mistake usually taxes only startup - except request-scoped providers (lesson 04)
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
